%N A399335 The binomial matrix of the swinging factorial (A056040). Square array read by ascending antidiagonals.
%C A399335 See the comments and links in A399000.
%H A399335 Peter Luschny, <a href="https://github.com/PeterLuschny/Gists/blob/main/GnomonicExpansionAndBinomialMatrices.ipynb">Gnomonic Expansion and Binomial Matrices</a>, a Python notebook.
%F A399335 A(n, n) = S(n) := n! / floor(n/2)!^2.
%F A399335 A(n, k) = Sum_{m=0..d} binomial(d, m) * s^(d - m) * S(p + m), where d = abs(n - k), p = min(n, k), s = 1 if k <= n, otherwise -1.
